/target/
plugins/*/src/bindings.rs
/.cache/
/.env
/.sqlx-tmp/
/web/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
node_modules/

# The same two names again, without the trailing slash.
#
# A pattern ending in `/` matches a directory and nothing else, so in a feature worktree —
# where `scripts/worktree.sh` links both of these into the main checkout — git sees a *symlink*
# named `web/dist`, decides it is not covered, and a `git add -A` commits it. The result is a
# link pointing at an absolute path on one machine, which then replaces the real directories
# the next time somebody merges. That happened once; these two lines are why it cannot again.
/web/dist
/web/node_modules
/data/
/artifacts/
*.part
*.rdplug
playwright-report/
test-results/
/dist/plugins/*.rdplug
# The browser extension is built into /artifacts/browser-extensions, which the line above
# already covers. `extension/dist/` was the output folder before that move and is no longer
# written by `extension/build.mjs`; the ignore entry only kept a stale second copy of the
# extension lying around for anyone loading it unpacked (RD-109-25). If one reappears, it is
# meant to be seen, not hidden.
/.claude/
.vscode